pan><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pomaks are Bulgarian-speaking Muslims living mainly in the Rhodope Mountains of Bulgaria and in neighbouring parts of Greece and Turkey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomare-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomare-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pōmare I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pōmare I, born Tū, was a Tahitian chief who founded the Pōmare dynasty and the Kingdom of Tahiti.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomare-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomare-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pōmare II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pōmare II was king of Tahiti, son of Pōmare I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomare-iv"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomare-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pōmare IV</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pōmare IV was queen of Tahiti for fifty years, from 1827 to 1877.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomare-v"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomare-v.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pōmare V</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pōmare V was the last king of Tahiti, reigning from 1877 to 1880.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomerania"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomerania.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pomerania</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pomerania is a historical region on the southern Baltic coast, today divided between Germany and Poland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-stettin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomerania-stettin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pomerania-Stettin</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">Pomerania-Stettin was a partition of the Duchy of Pomerania, created in 1295 for Otto I and ruled by a line of the Griffin dukes from Stettin (Szczecin).</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomerania-wolgast.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pomerania-Wolgast</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">Pomerania-Wolgast was a partition of the Duchy of Pomerania, created in 1295 for Bogislaw IV and ruled by Griffin dukes from Wolgast.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomeranians-slavic-tribe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomeranians-slavic-tribe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pomeranians (Slavic tribe)</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pomeranians were a West Slavic people who lived along the Baltic coast between the Oder and the Vistula in the early Middle Ages.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomerelia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomerelia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pomerelia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pomerelia, or Gdańsk Pomerania, is a historical region of northern Poland west of the lower Vistula, centred on Gdańsk.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pomorie"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pomorie.jpg